WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.830
(audience clapping)
- Martha made history

00:00:01.830 --> 00:00:04.710
with her Sports Illustrated
swimsuit issue cover

00:00:04.710 --> 00:00:06.065
at 81 years old.

00:00:06.065 --> 00:00:09.065
(audience cheering)

00:00:11.730 --> 00:00:13.350
First of all, ma'am.

00:00:13.350 --> 00:00:14.190
- [Guest] Goodness.

00:00:14.190 --> 00:00:16.650
- Every 81 year old out there is like,

00:00:16.650 --> 00:00:18.270
this is not like the others.

00:00:18.270 --> 00:00:20.937
Like this is like, it's in incre...

00:00:20.937 --> 00:00:21.840
Why now?

00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:23.280
Like, this is incredible.

00:00:23.280 --> 00:00:24.420
- I wonder.

00:00:24.420 --> 00:00:27.120
They never asked me before.

00:00:27.120 --> 00:00:28.680
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:00:28.680 --> 00:00:30.360
- I would've done it when I was 40.

00:00:30.360 --> 00:00:31.780
I looked great at 40.

00:00:31.780 --> 00:00:33.930
(Kelly chuckling)

00:00:33.930 --> 00:00:36.171
- Well, they think you
look great at 81 too.

00:00:36.171 --> 00:00:38.665
So it's just I love that you did it too.

00:00:38.665 --> 00:00:42.030
I think it was the most
popular one, right?

00:00:42.030 --> 00:00:42.863
- [Martha] Yeah.

00:00:42.863 --> 00:00:43.696
- Of the covers.

00:00:43.696 --> 00:00:46.350
- Yeah, we got like many,
many billions of impressions.

00:00:46.350 --> 00:00:47.183
- It was crazy.

00:00:48.863 --> 00:00:52.274
I do think though, you aged really well,

00:00:52.274 --> 00:00:54.934
so I don't know if that's
comparable to the rest of us,

00:00:54.934 --> 00:00:57.030
but I don't know.

00:00:57.030 --> 00:00:58.320
Did your mother influence you?

00:00:58.320 --> 00:01:00.420
Didn't she kind of influence
your attitude about aging?

00:01:00.420 --> 00:01:02.979
- Mom was great, and mom was beautiful,

00:01:02.979 --> 00:01:07.800
and with it, and totally
alert and intelligent,

00:01:07.800 --> 00:01:09.690
and she raised six kids.

00:01:09.690 --> 00:01:10.860
- No.

00:01:10.860 --> 00:01:14.730
- And she was great until the
day she passed away at 93, so.

00:01:14.730 --> 00:01:15.630
- [Kelly] 93.

00:01:15.630 --> 00:01:19.320
- And she's never sick,
and she was fantastic.

00:01:19.320 --> 00:01:20.760
She was swimming every day, you know,

00:01:20.760 --> 00:01:22.140
she's an amazing woman.

00:01:22.140 --> 00:01:23.194
- What a great role model as well.

00:01:23.194 --> 00:01:25.050
- Very, very good role model.

00:01:25.050 --> 00:01:27.390
- Well, you were following in
those footsteps, aren't ya,

00:01:27.390 --> 00:01:28.383
I was like, wow.

